WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:08.375
This is Anthropic, Read Aloud. Today: Building on our commitment to American scientific discovery.

2
00:00:09.675 --> 00:00:13.152
Building on our commitment to American scientific discovery.

3
00:00:13.602 --> 00:00:25.418
Anthropic is committing 150 dollarsmillion over three years to the Genesis Mission, a federal initiative to accelerate scientific and technological discovery through A I.

4
00:00:25.868 --> 00:00:30.279
From Anthropic Newsroom, published October 8, 2026.

5
00:00:31.279 --> 00:00:46.905
Anthropic is deepening its support for American scientific research by committing 150 dollarsmillion over three years to the Genesis Mission, a federal initiative to accelerate scientific and technological discovery through A I.

6
00:00:47.025 --> 00:00:58.242
The funding will go toward making Claude available to more than 15 agencies that are part of the mission, including NASA, the National Institutes of Health, and the National Science Foundation.

7
00:00:58.692 --> 00:01:11.727
We first announced our partnership with the U S Department of Energy (DOE) and the Genesis Mission last December. Since then, we have worked with DOE to bring Claude to scientists across the national laboratories.

8
00:01:11.847 --> 00:01:23.261
Today, we announced this new commitment as part of the Science: A New Golden Age Summit hosted by the White House Office of Science and Technology Policy in Washington, D C.

9
00:01:24.061 --> 00:01:25.945
Supporting American scientists.

10
00:01:26.395 --> 00:01:40.005
We share the administration’s view, laid out in “ Science: A New Golden Age,” that A I can have a profound and positive impact on scientific discovery, and we are glad to back its efforts to support American scientists.

11
00:01:40.455 --> 00:01:54.644
Researchers at federal agencies and national laboratories work on some of the world’s most difficult scientific problems. Through our commitment, we aim to help them use Claude to meaningfully advance their work. Over the next three years, we will:

12
00:01:55.094 --> 00:02:01.383
Provide Claude, Claude Code, and A P I credits to several hundred Genesis Mission research projects.

13
00:02:01.623 --> 00:02:11.538
Partner closely with agencies and national laboratories on the administration’s top science priorities, including fusion energy and quantum computing; and.

14
00:02:11.778 --> 00:02:22.339
Provide training, onboarding, and technical support to scientists on Genesis Mission projects, and help agencies new to the Genesis Mission get their first projects running.

15
00:02:23.139 --> 00:02:25.112
Accelerating scientific research.

16
00:02:25.562 --> 00:02:42.988
This commitment is part of our broader effort to support scientific research. Earlier this year we launched Claude Science, an A I workbench that integrates the tools and packages researchers most commonly use, and opened 10000 free and discounted Claude seats for academic scientists.

17
00:02:43.108 --> 00:03:03.409
We also expanded our A I for Science program, which gives credits to researchers on high-impact projects, and kicked off a research preview of the Model Hardware Standard, a shared specification for A I agents to safely operate lab instruments. Our commitment to the Genesis Mission is our next step toward helping researchers everywhere.

18
00:03:04.409 --> 00:03:22.472
That was Building on our commitment to American scientific discovery, from Anthropic Newsroom, published October 8, 2026. Read the original at anthropic dot com. This unofficial audio edition was generated automatically for the podcast Anthropic, Read Aloud.
